2026-07-08T10:53:34.291Z [DEBUG] "Hook SessionStart:startup (SessionStart) success:\n=== REMEMBER ===\nHistory in .remember/: now.md (buffer), today-*.md (daily), recent.md (7d), archive.md (old), core-memories.md (key moments). Search on user request.\n\n=== MEMORY ===\n--- now.md ---\n\n## F001 a105413b baseline BEFORE capture — COMPLETE (2026-07-07)\n- librccl.so rebuilt (gfx950, 29MB) via install.sh --amdgpu_targets gfx950; earlier build dir had no .so (OOM-killed rebuild).\n- LESSON: never run two install.sh in the same rccl build/ tree — they race on fmt FetchContent and break CMake configure (\"Build step for fmt failed\"). Kill duplicates, then a single clean build reuses cached device .o files.\n- topo_expl -m 59 confirms 8xgfx950 XGMI clique (nranks=8, 56 max channels). topo_expl_impl.cpp fix (zero cpu host_hash) required for gfx950 fixture.\n- All 5 sweeps (allreduce half/bf16, reducescatter, allgather, alltoall) captured 8B..2GiB, exit=0, #wrong==0, saved to projects/rccl/perf_results/baseline/.\n- Size ceiling 2G (not 8G AC): GPU3 has external vLLM tenant occupying ~293GB; -e 4G/8G OOM. Documented in ENV.txt.\n\n## T4 0e44d83e recursive-halving/doubling DDA (RHD) — COMPLETE (2026-07-07)\n- LESSON (CRITICAL for any DDA/IPC feature): DDA IPC paths (RHD, dda_all_reduce, dda_reduce_scatter, etc.) are SKIPPED when comm is in directMode. ncclTransportCheckP2pType sets directMode=1 whenever two local ranks share a pid — i.e. any single-process `rccl-tests -g 8` run. ncclDdaIpcCommInit then skips scratch/barrier alloc, so gate-on == gate-off (both fall back to ring). To honestly measure ANY DDA feature you MUST run 1 process per GPU: build rccl-tests with `make MPI=1 NAME_SUFFIX=_mpi GPU_TARGETS=gfx950 MPI_HOME=/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu NCCL_HOME=<rccl>/build/release CUSTOM_RCCL_LIB=<same>` then `mpirun -np 8 <coll>_perf_mpi -g 1`. Verify engagement via NCCL_DEBUG=INFO NCCL_DEBUG_SUBSYS=COLL,INIT -> expect \"RCCL RHD ...\" on all 8 ranks and \"directMode 0\".\n- SETUP: libopenmpi-dev was not installed; `sudo apt-get install -y libopenmpi-dev` (passwordless sudo available). Headers land at /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/openmpi/include/mpi.h, libs at .../openmpi/lib — matches rccl-tests src/Makefile MPI paths.\n- RESULT (honest, negative): RHD is bit-exact (#wrong==0, fp32/fp16/bf16) but ~5-6x SLOWER than ring/tree on 8xMI355X XGMI clique across 256K-64M (AR 64M 379->61 GB/s, RS 361->61). Cause: full XGMI clique is bandwidth-bound not latency-bound, so RHD's fewer-rounds bet doesn't pay; extra IPC-scratch copy + fine-grained IPC round-trips dominate. Left default-off (RCCL_RHD_ENABLE=0), NOT force-enabled. Report: projects/rccl/perf_results/T4_rhd.md; raw MPI sweeps in perf_results/t4/mpi_*.txt. Single-process t4/{ar,rs}_{off,on}.txt are stale (RHD never engaged).\n- Enum: RCCL_RECURSIVE_HALVING added at rccl_common.h:63 (after RCCL_SYMMETRIC, before RCCL_ALGO_COUNT) — RCCL-local, doesn't perturb NCCL enum. tuning.cc latCount term is gated on ncclRhdEnabled() so it's a no-op when off.\n\n\n"
